WEBVTT

00:04.000 --> 00:08.000 line:94% position:50% align:center size:90%
CAML learns a scalar energy whose low-energy set represents a supplied spatial manifold.

00:08.000 --> 00:12.000 line:94% position:50% align:center size:90%
The energy gradient restores perturbed activity toward the manifold.

00:12.000 --> 00:16.000 line:94% position:50% align:center size:90%
A separately learned bump-shifting field responds to velocity inputs.

00:16.000 --> 00:28.000 line:94% position:50% align:center size:90%
The energy gradient restores perturbed states toward ring and torus manifolds.

00:28.000 --> 00:40.000 line:94% position:50% align:center size:90%
Head-direction activity recovers a localized bump as population energy decreases.

00:40.000 --> 00:52.000 line:94% position:50% align:center size:90%
Grid-cell activity recovers a localized bump on the rhombic lattice.

00:52.000 --> 01:04.000 line:94% position:50% align:center size:90%
Angular velocity moves the head-direction bump along the learned ring.

01:04.000 --> 01:16.000 line:94% position:50% align:center size:90%
Linear velocity translates grid activity along its two phase directions.
